{
  "title": "Enforce trade document authority independently of the MVC request pipeline",
  "description": "Stage 3 verified authorization-path gap, a direct continuation of ERP-394 and the same defect class as ERP-462 to ERP-493. [TradeDocumentRequestAuthorizationFilter] is the only authority on four trade-document generation entries (src/ERP.Api/Controllers/SalesOrderController.cs:898 and :937, src/ERP.Api/Controllers/ContainerLoadingListController.cs:176 and :213) and on all of src/ERP.Api/Controllers/TradeDocumentController.cs:32; the filter (TradeDocumentController.cs:525-545, IAsyncActionFilter) runs only inside the MVC pipeline, while the actions read ScopeFrom(HttpContext) (TradeDocumentController.cs:46-47 and :557-560) which returns null when the scope item is absent, and src/ERP.Application/Services/TradeDocumentAuthorizationRules.cs:137-143 ScopeFilter returns a match-all predicate for a null scope, so an in-process call resolves no live identity, no ERP-453 account status, no existing doc-center (单证中心) menu and no ERP-097 customer scope and can read, print, export, mutate and generate trade documents and their line snapshots (TradeDocumentController CRUD / print / export-excel / items, SalesOrderController.TradeDocumentPrefill:899-926 and GenerateTradeDocuments:938-961, ContainerLoadingListController.TradeDocumentPrefill:177-202 and GenerateTradeDocuments:214-236). Resolve the existing live authorization (TradeDocumentAuthorizationRules.EnsureMenuAuthorizedAsync:99) inside every one of those routes and use the returned non-null scope, remove the pipeline-shape waiver and its ScopeItemKey plumbing, and keep every existing boundary: persisted TradeDocument.CustomerId ownership, source customer and generated-target authorization via TradeDocumentGeneration, line-snapshot and status-freeze semantics, and zero writes on denial. Adapt the legacy in-process trade-document fixtures to genuine enabled identities holding their existing doc-center grant in isolated test data only. No new menu, grant, permission, table or column, no anonymous, administrative, environment or test-only fallback, and no report or unrelated-module change. Safe Release build plus full ERP.UnitTests; genuine SQL only on the isolated localdb NEWERP_AutoAcceptance instance with a fresh GUID-owned NEWERP_AUTOTEST database. Preserve current business permissions and actor/customer scope; no new grants. Adapt all affected original fixtures with real enabled identities and existing menus/master rows, never remove business assertions or retain null-context/provider/test exceptions. Full original failure logs retained. Explicit test output/TRX/results directories must be .ai/logs/<task> only, never repository-root TestResults. SQL must use exactly (localdb)\\NEWERP_AutoAcceptance with Integrated Security and a fresh GUID-owned NEWERP_AUTOTEST database; reject wrong/existing targets before access, never drop/reset. Safe Release restore/build with analyzers and warnings-as-errors, full units and relevant genuine isolated SQL validation; no whole-stage acceptance or production access.",
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "Every trade document entry (all /api/trade/documents routes including paged, all, by-id, create, update, delete, batch-delete, print, export-excel and line-item read/write/delete, plus /api/sales-orders/{id}/trade-documents/prefill, /api/sales-orders/{id}/trade-documents, /api/container/loading-lists/{id}/trade-documents/prefill and /api/container/loading-lists/{id}/trade-documents) resolves the current live enabled nondeleted identity, the ERP-453 account status and the existing doc-center (单证中心) menu through TradeDocumentAuthorizationRules.EnsureMenuAuthorizedAsync before any count, document row, snapshot, workbook byte or write, independently of whether HttpContext is bound, whether Request.Path is set and whether the call passes through the MVC filter pipeline; the TradeDocumentRequestAuthorizationFilter application and its ScopeFrom plumbing are removed, missing/zero/unknown/deleted identity fails Unauthorized, disabled identity and missing/revoked menu fail Forbidden, and no anonymous, administrative, environment or test-only fallback is added.",
    "Retain the existing trade document boundaries and response contracts: the resolved non-null scope is pushed down to SQL before count and paging, document ownership stays the persisted TradeDocument.CustomerId, source-owner and generated-target authorization keeps using TradeDocumentGeneration guards, item line snapshots and the submitted-customer/used status freeze stay unchanged, and every denied route reads or writes zero TradeDocuments, TradeDocumentItems or trade-document number sequence rows, with no new menu, grant, permission, table or column.",
    "Adapt the legacy in-process trade-document fixtures to genuine enabled identities holding their existing doc-center menu grants in isolated test data only, and add genuine unit plus isolated SQL controller tests covering the trade document register, the item routes and the four sales-order / loading-list generation entries for missing/zero/deleted identity, disabled and revoked-menu identity, limited-scope identity reading an out-of-scope document or source, no-HttpContext calls with empty and populated Request.Path, and permitted flows; existing TradeDocumentAuthorizationTests, TradeDocumentItemTests, TradeDocumentMutationTests, TradeDocumentLineSnapshotTests, TradeDocumentGenerationTests and TradeDocumentGenerationMutationTests plus their SQL counterparts stay green.",
    "Keep the safe Release build with analyzers and warnings-as-errors and the full existing ERP.UnitTests suite green, run genuine SQL only on the isolated localdb NEWERP_AutoAcceptance instance with Integrated Security and a fresh GUID-owned NEWERP_AUTOTEST database that is never dropped or reset, and claim no whole-stage acceptance from a build alone."
  ],
